small_code_examples:
Example client headers (TypeScript SDK helper):

// TypeScript: attach a retry token for a resumed stream
headers['x-redwood-retry-token'] = generateOpaqueRetryToken();
headers['x-redwood-idempotency-session'] = sessionId;

Server-surface: HTTP headers recognized by the runtime:
X-Redwood-Retry-Token: <opaque-base64>  // short-lived, server-checked
X-Redwood-Idempotency-Session: <session-uuid> // sequences frames, optional

Behavior notes: when a stream reconnects with both headers, the runtime attempts safe resume: it will return a short resume frame indicating the last-committed sequence index. If the retry token is missing, runtime uses exponential backoff hints (Retry-After) but will not allow at-most-once guarantees for side-effect frames.
